"comparison":"Both MU and AMD disclose customer concentration metrics for 2024, but they measure different financial exposures: MU reports revenue concentration where one customer reached the 10% threshold, whereas AMD reports accounts receivable concentration where one customer exceeded 20%. MU states that 'Revenue from one customer was 10% (primarily included in MBU, EBU, and CNBU segments) of total revenue for 2024,' while AMD notes that 'One customer accounted for approximately 24% and another customer accounted for 16% of the total consolidated accounts receivable balance as of December 28, 2024 and December 30, 2023, respectively.' Additionally, MU explicitly states no customer hit the 10% revenue threshold in 2023, contrasting with the new concentration in 2024.",
