"relationship":"same_topic",
"comparison":"Both MU and AVGO disclose significant customer concentration affecting both revenue and receivables in 2024, with AVGO showing a much higher concentration level than MU. MU reports that 'Revenue from one customer was 10% (primarily included in MBU, EBU, and CNBU segments) of total revenue for 2024,' while AVGO discloses that 'One customer accounted for 18% and 21% of our net accounts receivable balance as of November 3, 2024 and October 29, 2023, respectively' and 'During fiscal years 2024, 2023 and 2022, one customer accounted for 28%, 21% and 20% of our net revenue, respectively.' Both companies identify a single customer as a major concentration risk, but AVGO's exposure is more pronounced in both revenue share (28% vs 10%) and receivables.",
