"comparison":"Both MU and INTC address customer concentration in 2024, but INTC does not quantify the percentage of revenue from its largest customers, instead noting that 'In 2024, substantially all of the revenue from our three largest customers was from the sale of platforms and other components by our Intel Products operating segments.' In contrast, MU provides specific quantitative thresholds, stating 'Revenue from one customer was 10% (primarily included in MBU, EBU, and CNBU segments) of total revenue for 2024.' While both disclose that significant revenue is derived from a small number of customers, MU offers precise percentage data whereas INTC provides qualitative source attribution.",
